# Every nameplate calling the duty-cycle question malformed, beside whether its unit runs on a
# period. One row per examined nameplate, `violates` where the unit does have one.
#
# `notApplicable` only where the unit has no period
#   The rule: a window is notApplicable only where the unit has no period. `12 people` has no
#   period, so "five days" has nothing to be five days of and the question really is malformed.
#   `4 GPU-hours per week` has one, so the question is perfectly answerable, and `notApplicable`
#   there is a refusal dressed as a category error.
#
# A nameplate with no unit is not examined
#   That is the repair. `refutation`'s `object-storage` files its amount `notApplicable` (there
#   is no unit at all) and its window `notApplicable` too. A NULL unit matches no `LIKE`, so a
#   semi-join against a parsed denominator passes it, on the grounds that a unit which does not
#   exist has no denominator. That is an unknown answered as a no. layers/absorber.sqlc states
#   the principle: a question nobody can answer gets no row rather than a pass.
#
# The semi-join reads a filed fact, never a parsed one
#   Against free text, `LIKE '% per %' OR LIKE '% por %'` guesses the denominator out of the unit
#   string and silently decides that `semana` is `week`: a reader's judgement written in SQL,
#   which no comment on the query side can fix.
#
#   It is also the wrong predicate: a `LIKE` finds a denominator, and this rule needs a period.
#   `pm:StatedDenominator` separates them, so the semi-join is against units/with_a_period.sqlc
#   and `GPU-hour per GPU` does not count as a rate.
-- pm:Divisibility/window with pm:absent/reason = notApplicable, against pm:Claim/pm:denominator.
SELECT r.rule, p.filing, p.layer, p.violates, p.detail
FROM      (
    :compose(checks/roster.sqlc)
) r
LEFT JOIN (
    SELECT w.filing, w.layer,
           r.filing IS NOT NULL AS violates,
           CASE WHEN r.filing IS NOT NULL
                THEN format('%s runs on a period, so the duty cycle question is answerable',
                            w.amount_unit)
                ELSE format('%s has no period under the line, so the question really is malformed',
                            w.amount_unit)
           END AS detail
    FROM      (
        :compose(layers/windows.sqlc)
    ) w
    LEFT JOIN (
        :compose(units/with_a_period.sqlc)
    ) r USING (filing, layer)
    WHERE w.window_absent = 'notApplicable'
      AND w.amount_unit IS NOT NULL
) p ON true
WHERE r.slug = 'window_not_applicable_on_a_rate'
